    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb36034Cx",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "As the current MP for Northcote, I am standing again to continue fixing the basics and building a better, brighter, more prosperous and safer future for our community and country. I have the skills and experience needed to contribute effectively in Parliament and stand for no new taxes, personal responsibility, fiscal discipline, a thriving private sector and a government that focuses on delivering the basics well. "
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb36034I1",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "Parliament is heavy on lawyers and people who have worked in politics, but light on professional economists and people with real-world commercial experience (other than in National). I am a qualified butcher, a Harvard-trained economist, and someone who brings over 15 years' experience working in the private sector and in economic roles in NZ, Europe and Asia. I love the Northcote electorate and will continue to work hard for you."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb36034N5",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Ensure we grow our economy so that you and your family can get ahead in our community. "
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb36034S9",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Lead the Northcote Community Safety Forum so that crime continues to fall in our community."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb36034XD",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Keep pushing for practical solutions to reduce congestion (e.g. yellow lines on Onewa Rd)."
     }
    ],
