   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb36035g7",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "This election is about a better future for our community. Too many people feel the government has lost focus on the issues that matter most. The cost of living is too expensive; people can't access healthcare when they need it and we've lost amazing social services. Better is possible. But there is so much more to do, and that is why I am standing for Northcote in 2026. Better for Northcote starts now."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb36035lB",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I love this community; it has been my home for 20+ years. I'm proud to have fought and delivered for this community: more classrooms, more hospital beds, better public transport and investment in local services. I've had the privilege to be a listening ear and the voice fighting for our community in parliament against this government. Now, I want to take my passion for our community and the things I have learnt to deliver again."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb36035qF",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Deliver more nurses at North Shore Hospital, so our community can get care when they need it most."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb36035vJ",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Provide cost of living relief for Northcote, because right now too many families are struggling."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb360360N",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Create real and accessible opportunities for young people, to help everyone build a future here."
     }
    ],
